<title>UK: 2nd UK-Americas/Africa/Nordic air cargo report.</title>
<headline>2nd UK-Americas/Africa/Nordic air cargo report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>This is Reuters' 2nd ex-UK air cargo market report which only covers the America, Africa and the Nordic countries.</p>
<p>This report and one covering the ex-UK market to Asia/Australasia/MidEast will be issued on alternate weeks.</p>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK air cargo rates to the United States, Latin America, Africa and Scandinavia per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>			 Mar 3	 Feb 13</p>
<p>		  UNITED STATES</p>
<p> LON-JFK	 0.63		 0.65</p>
<p> LON-LAX	 0.80		 0.80</p>
<p> LON-CHI	 0.74		 0.76</p>
<p>		  LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> LON-SAO	 2.10		 2.10</p>
<p> LON-BUE	 2.21		 2.19</p>
<p>		  AFRICA</p>
<p> LON-JNB	 1.63		 1.65</p>
<p> LON-NBO	 0.93		 0.95</p>
<p>		  SCANDINAVIA</p>
<p> LON-STO	 0.73		 0.75</p>
<p> LON-CPH	 0.70		 0.70</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax +5017</p>
</text>
